    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="1314" n="1156" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1156"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Gummeré</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-11-06"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 60.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 1, of September 29 last, describing your visit to the court at Fez,
                    and transmitting copies of your address on the occasion of the presentation to
                    the Sultan of the letter addressed to him by the President and His Majesty’s
                    reply.</p>
                <pb facs="1315" n="1157" xml:id="pg1157"/>
                <p>Your dispatch has been read with much gratification, and the department avails
                    itself with pleasure of the opportunity to express its confidence that this
                    manifestation of the friendly regard of the Government and people of the United
                    States for the Shereefian Empire will beneficially, inure to the mutual
                    relations of the two countries.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
